workedExamples.solution_text:
Place $M$ directly below the highest point of the curve. The mode corresponds to its single peak.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm]
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(6,0);\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,3.2);\draw[thick,black] (0.2,0.1)..controls (0.6,0.2) and (0.7,2.8)..(1.5,2.8)..controls (2.3,2.8) and (2.2,0.2)..(5.6,0.1);
\draw[dashed,draw={rgb,255:red,38;green,140;blue,255}] (1.5,0)--(1.5,2.8);
\node[text={rgb,255:red,38;green,140;blue,255},below,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] at (1.5,0) {$M$};
\node[below,black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] at (3,-0.4) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
